---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

const title = '10 Signs Your Website Needs a Redesign';
const description = 'Is your website helping or hurting your business? Here are 10 warning signs that your site is due for an overhaul.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <Navbar />
  <article class="blog-post">
    <div class="hero-bg">
      <div class="gradient-blob blob-1"></div>
      <div class="gradient-blob blob-2"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="container">
      <header class="post-header reveal">
        <div class="post-meta">
          <span class="post-category">Web Design</span>
          <span class="post-date">April 2026 · 7 min read</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="post-title">10 Signs Your Website Needs a Redesign (And What to Do About It)</h1>
        <p class="post-excerpt">Is your website helping or hurting your business? Here are 10 warning signs that your site is due for an overhaul — plus a roadmap to fix it.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="post-content reveal">
        <p class="lead">Your website is your 24/7 salesperson. If it is not working while you sleep, it is working against you. Here are the 10 signs that tell you it is time for a redesign.</p>

        <h2>1. Your Site Takes More Than 3 Seconds to Load</h2>
        <p>Google research is clear: 53% of mobile visitors abandon a page that takes longer than 3 seconds to load. If your site is slow, you are losing half your potential customers before they even see your offer. Test your speed with Google PageSpeed Insights.</p>

        <h2>2. It Is Not Mobile-Friendly</h2>
        <p>Over 60% of web traffic is mobile. If your site requires pinch-to-zoom, has buttons too small to tap, or breaks on phones, you are telling the majority of your visitors to leave. Mobile-first is not a trend — it is the default.</p>

        <h2>3. You Are Not Getting Leads</h2>
        <p>A beautiful website with zero leads is an expensive decoration. If your contact forms sit empty and your phone does not ring, your site has a conversion problem. This is usually due to weak CTAs, confusing navigation, or no clear value proposition.</p>

        <h2>4. Your Competitors Outrank You</h2>
        <p>Search "your service + your city." If you are not on page one, your website is invisible to 95% of searchers. Poor SEO architecture, slow speed, thin content, and missing structured data all hurt rankings.</p>

        <h2>5. The Design Looks Dated</h2>
        <p>Web design trends evolve. A site that looked modern in 2019 looks ancient today. Dated design signals to visitors that your business might be dated too. First impressions form in 50 milliseconds — and they are hard to undo.</p>

        <h2>6. Your Bounce Rate Is Above 70%</h2>
        <p>Bounce rate measures visitors who leave without interacting. A high bounce rate means your site is not delivering what visitors expect. Common causes: slow load times, misleading headlines, poor design, or unclear value propositions.</p>

        <h2>7. You Cannot Update Content Yourself</h2>
        <p>If every blog post, photo change, or text edit requires a developer, your website is a bottleneck. Modern sites use CMS platforms that let non-technical users manage content easily.</p>

        <h2>8. It Does Not Reflect Your Current Business</h2>
        <p>Businesses evolve. Services change. Team members come and go. If your website still shows offerings you retired two years ago, it is actively confusing potential customers.</p>

        <h2>9. No Analytics or Tracking</h2>
        <p>If you cannot answer "how many visitors did we get last month?" or "what is our most popular page?" you are flying blind. Data-driven decisions require data. A modern website has analytics baked in from day one.</p>

        <h2>10. You Are Embarrassed to Share Your URL</h2>
        <p>This is the most honest sign of all. If you hesitate to send someone to your website, it is not doing its job. Your website should be your best salesperson — not a source of shame.</p>

        <h2>What to Do Next</h2>
        <p>If 3 or more of these apply to you, it is time to act. Here is the priority order:</p>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Audit your current site.</strong> Use free tools like PageSpeed Insights, GTmetrix, and Google Search Console.</li>
          <li><strong>Define your goals.</strong> What should your website accomplish? Leads? Sales? Awareness?</li>
          <li><strong>Set a budget.</strong> Be realistic about what a quality site costs. (See our pricing breakdown.)</li>
          <li><strong>Find the right partner.</strong> Look for someone who asks about your goals, not just your colors.</li>
          <li><strong>Plan the content.</strong> Great design with weak copy is still a weak site.</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="cta-box">
          <h3>Get a Free Website Audit</h3>
          <p>We will review your site and send you a 5-minute video showing exactly what is broken and how to fix it. Completely free.</p>
          <a href="/book-call" class="cta-button">Request Free Audit</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="post-footer reveal">
        <div class="post-tags"><span>Web Design</span><span>Redesign</span><span>Audit</span></div>
        <a href="/blog" class="back-link"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M19 12H5"/><path d="M12 19l-7-7 7-7"/></svg>Back to Blog</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .blog-post { padding: 140px 0 80px; position: relative; overflow: hidden; background: var(--bg-primary); min-height: 100vh; }
  .hero-bg { position: absolute; inset: 0; overflow: hidden; }
  .gradient-blob { position: absolute; border-radius: 50%; filter: blur(120px); opacity: 0.3; }
  .blob-1 { width: 400px; height: 400px; background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(59,130,246,0.3), transparent 70%); top: 5%; right: -10%; }
  .blob-2 { width: 300px; height: 300px; background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(139,92,246,0.25), transparent 70%); bottom: 20%; left: -5%; }
  .post-header { position: relative; z-index: 1; max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto 60px; text-align: center; }
  .post-meta { display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 16px; margin-bottom: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .post-category { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent-primary); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
  .post-date { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .post-title { font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 52px); font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.1; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .post-excerpt { font-size: 18px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .post-content { position: relative; z-index: 1; max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .post-content .lead { font-size: 20px; color: var(--text-primary); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 40px; }
  .post-content h2 { font-size: 28px; font-weight: 700; margin: 48px 0 20px; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .post-content h3 { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; margin: 32px 0 12px; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .post-content p { font-size: 16px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .post-content ul, .post-content ol { margin: 0 0 24px 24px; }
  .post-content li { font-size: 16px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .post-content li strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .cta-box { background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(59,130,246,0.08) 0%, rgba(17,24,39,0.5) 100%); border: 1px solid rgba(59,130,246,0.2); border-radius: var(--radius-xl); padding: 40px; margin: 40px 0; text-align: center; }
  .cta-box h3 { font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 12px; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .cta-box p { font-size: 16px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .cta-button { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; padding: 16px 32px; background: var(--accent-primary); color: white; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; border-radius: var(--radius-md); transition: all 0.35s var(--transition); box-shadow: 0 4px 24px rgba(59,130,246,0.3); }
  .cta-button:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(59,130,246,0.4); }
  .post-footer { max-width: 720px; margin: 60px auto 0; padding-top: 40px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 20px; }
  .post-tags { display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .post-tags span { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 6px 14px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04); border-radius: 100px; }
  .back-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent-primary); transition: gap 0.3s; }
  .back-link:hover { gap: 12px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .blog-post { padding: 120px 0 60px; }
    .post-title { font-size: 28px; }
    .post-content .lead { font-size: 18px; }
    .post-content h2 { font-size: 24px; }
    .cta-box { padding: 28px 24px; }
    .gradient-blob { display: none; }
  }
</style>